tone — a sine through the sound graph

  tone                   one second of concert pitch
  tone 1000              a chosen frequency, in hertz
  tone 1000 250          and a chosen length, in milliseconds

The simplest thing that makes sound: one node, one output port, linked
to whatever `patch` says the default sink is. What it proves is
everything beneath it, so it is the first thing to run when a machine
is silent and should not be.

Silence from `tone` with no complaint means the graph carried it and
the hardware did not: check `vol`, then `patch` for where the link
went.
